<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- English strings for REFUGIO.admx. Goes in PolicyDefinitions\en-US\. -->
<policyDefinitionResources revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0">
  <displayName>REFUGIO</displayName>
  <description>Policies for REFUGIO, a private AI assistant that runs locally.</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="REFUGIO">REFUGIO</string>

      <string id="DisableWebSearch">Turn off web search</string>
      <string id="DisableWebSearch_Help">Web search is the only feature of REFUGIO that sends anything off the computer. It is off by default, and even when a user switches it on, each individual message has to be armed for search separately, with a warning shown at the time.

Enabled: the user cannot switch web search on at all. The control in Settings is disabled and says it was set by your organisation.

Disabled or Not Configured: the user decides.

There is deliberately no policy that turns web search on. Arming a search is a decision made by the person at the keyboard, in front of a warning, and REFUGIO will not make it on their behalf.</string>

      <string id="DisableUpdateChecks">Turn off update checks</string>
      <string id="DisableUpdateChecks_Help">REFUGIO can check whether a newer version exists by asking github.com what commit a public branch points at. No user data is sent — not messages, not a version, not an identifier.

Enabled: REFUGIO makes no update requests at all, including the manual "Check now" button.

Set this on a managed fleet where updates arrive through your deployment tool. Otherwise REFUGIO will tell users an update is available and show them a command they have no rights to run.</string>

      <string id="DisableAttachments">Turn off file attachments</string>
      <string id="DisableAttachments_Help">Files attached to a message are copied into the user's profile and their text is read into the prompt. Everything stays on the computer.

Enabled: the attach control is removed from the chat. It disappears rather than refusing when pressed — a button that is present and rejects reads as a broken feature.

Disabled or Not Configured: the user may attach files.</string>

      <string id="AllowedModes">Limit which discussion modes may be offered</string>
      <string id="AllowedModes_Help">A comma-separated list of discussion mode ids. Discussion modes are built-in coaching frames for one conversation — NVC Coach, Style Coach, Career Coach, Life Coach, the Spanish Tutor, and a read-only mode for the user's own WhatsApp history. Every one of them is off until the user switches it on, and the conversation stays on the computer: a mode never searches the web and never sends anything on the user's behalf.

The ids are:  nvc, styles, whatsapp, spanish, career, life

For example:  nvc, career

Only the modes listed here may be switched on. Any other mode is forced off and its control in Settings is disabled, saying it was set by your organisation.

Leave this policy Not Configured to allow all of them. To take the feature away entirely, set a list that names no real mode — for example:  none

There is deliberately no policy that switches a mode ON. A coaching conversation is one a person chooses to have.</string>

      <string id="AllowedConnectors">Limit which connectors may run</string>
      <string id="AllowedConnectors_Help">A comma-separated list of connector ids. Only these are started; anything else in the configuration is never launched.

For example:  notes, reminders

Leave this policy Not Configured to allow every connector that is installed.

This is enforced where connectors are started, not where they are displayed — a connector excluded here is not running at all, rather than running and hidden.</string>
    </stringTable>

    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="AllowedModes">
        <textBox refId="AllowedModesText">
          <label>Mode ids, comma-separated</label>
          <defaultValue>nvc, career</defaultValue>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>

      <presentation id="AllowedConnectors">
        <textBox refId="AllowedConnectorsText">
          <label>Connector ids, comma-separated</label>
          <defaultValue>notes, reminders</defaultValue>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
